{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/997290-oddmageddon-the-end-of-prophecies","id":997290,"title":"Oddmageddon, The End of Prophecies!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-02T11:56:44-07:00","id":997290,"title":"Oddmageddon, The End of Prophecies!","content":"Well, I decided to make this into a separate thread, wish it goes well.<br /> <br /> For a chronicle I'm going to run, I'm thinking about this concept. There are the many, many possible truths of the World of Darkness. There is the world from the &quot;main&quot; POV of each splat, and sometimes the POVs of minor groups within each line. There is everything the WoD could be, if at least it could be at the same time. And there are the things the WoD could be, but never was before.<br /> <br /> Then it all start to crumble. The ancient precursors of the race of the undead raise to slake their vicious thirst on this damned world. Somewhere they are 13, elsewhere they are 21, and in at least one place Set, the First Vampire, tries to gather the ungrateful horde of its sworn enemies against the true danger of Wyrm/Apophis and the false blood gods. The werewolves gather to weather against 20 versions of the Last Battleground as the Hydra reaches fully into the world to destroy it once and for all. Reality itself fights against factions of witches and scientists, each working hard toward the goal of ultimate ascension.<br /> <br /> In the middle of the maelstrom, the Apocalypse, the Gehenna, the Winter, a rift opens between worlds. The last moment of the world happens, as prophecized so many ages before. And all of a sudden, it all... changes.<br /> <br /> Oddmageddon is the end of the world as no one could imagine before. All of a sudden, a hundred world collapse and fold into one another. And suddenly the prophecies of old are rendered moot and void. Even the powerful creatures that raised were not prepared for one another, and for the even more unexpected ones to appear. It isn't evil chaos. Nor is it destructive chaos. Just true, complete and untamed chaos, as the world is ravaged by weirdness and nothing is as expected.<br /> <br /> How would this be, when the world ends not in fire, ice or water, but in weirdness? How could the Oddmageddon unfold, and how would it end? What kind of interesting escape would there be for a group of PCs, for once, to bring a modicum of stability to the resultant world? And what will be the world that is left at its end?<br /> <br /> Nothing will be the same after the entire universe enters this twilight zone. There are no bounds, just infinite possibilities for ideas.<br /> <br /> As a side note, by myself I'm intended on using the CoD system afterwards. Either way, every suggestion for rules, both for the event as for the new world, are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:59:08-07:00","id":997321,"title":"","content":"I've taken a more basic approach to this with simply making Caine, Satan and Lilith separate factions trying to overthrow the Elohim in various ways and actually having a chance. Even that made the game very complicated to run and plan for, so I'd say the main obstacle would be the enormous amount of work combining and streamlining mechanics and backstories would take. With that said if you think you've got the time and will for that then go for it, create something distinctive and unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","user":"ElizabethSterling","date":". 11-02-2016, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}